    {
      "_id": "5vl6RZoSUXLJN2Iq",
      "name": "Bite",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/sword.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p><em>Melee Weapon Attack:</em> +10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. <em>Hit:</em>20 (2d12 + 7) piercing and 13 ([[/damage 2d12 poison]]). If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw or be swallowed by the plague-dog. A swallowed creature is blinded and restrained, has total cover against attacks and other effects outside the worm, and takes 21 ([[/damage 6d6 poison]]) at the start of each of the plague dog's turns. A plague dog can have only one creature swallowed at a time.\n\nIf the plague dog takes 30 damage or more on a single turn from the swallowed creature, the plague-dog must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or the creature successfully cuts its way through the dog and falls prone in a space within 5 feet of the plague-dog. If the plague-dog dies, a swallowed creature is no longer restrained by it and can escape from the corpse by using 15 feet of movement, exiting prone.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
